<html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><style>
body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 28px}
h1{font-size:22pt;color:#111827;border-bottom:3px solid #c5a028;padding-bottom:8px;margin-bottom:4px}
h2{font-size:14pt;color:#111827;margin-top:30px;margin-bottom:4px;border-left:4px solid #4fd1c5;padding-left:12px;background:#f4fdfc}
h3{font-size:12pt;color:#374151;margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:bold}
p{margin:4px 0 10px}
.meta{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 18px;margin-bottom:24px;font-size:10pt}
.meta p{margin:3px 0}
.meta strong{color:#b7881c}
.sec{border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;margin-top:28px;padding-top:16px}
.badge{display:inline-block;background:#ecfdf5;color:#065f46;font-size:9pt;font-weight:bold;padding:3px 12px;border-radius:20px;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px}
.card{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:10px 0}
.card-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11.5pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 4px}
.card-sub{font-size:10pt;color:#6b7280;margin:0 0 4px;font-style:italic}
.card-desc{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.step{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 14px;background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;margin:8px 0}
.step-num{font-size:18pt;font-weight:bold;color:#c5a028;min-width:40px;line-height:1}
.step-body .step-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 3px}
.step-body .step-desc{font-size:10.5pt;color:#374151;margin:0}
.faq{border-left:3px solid #4fd1c5;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0;background:#f9fafb;border-radius:0 6px 6px 0}
.faq-q{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;margin:0 0 5px}
.faq-a{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.cta{background:#111827;color:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 24px;margin-top:28px}
.cta h2{color:#4fd1c5;border:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 8px;background:transparent;font-size:15pt}
.cta p{color:#d1d5db;margin:4px 0}
.cta .btn{display:inline-block;background:#4fd1c5;color:#111827;font-weight:bold;padding:7px 16px;border-radius:5px;margin-top:8px;font-size:10pt}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0;font-size:10.5pt}
td{padding:7px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb}
td:first-child{color:#6b7280}
td:last-child{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;text-align:right}
ul{padding-left:18px}
ul li{padding:2px 0;color:#374151}
</style></head><body><h1>Refinance Calculator</h1><div class="meta"><p><strong>Page Title:</strong> Refinance Break-Even Calculator | Madison, WI | Rob Miller</p><p><strong>Meta Description:</strong> Calculate your refinance savings, monthly payments, and break-even point in Madison, WI. Get a personalized refinance strategy from Rob Miller. Licensed in 11 states.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>Hero Section</h2><h3>Refinance Break-Even Calculator</h3><p>Determine if refinancing makes sense for you. Estimate your new payment, see your monthly savings, and calculate exactly how many months it will take to break even on your closing costs.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>Main Page Content</h2><h3>Should You Refinance?</h3><h4>Get a Detailed Refinance Analysis</h4><p>Refinancing can be a powerful wealth-building tool if timed correctly. The most common reasons homeowners choose to refinance in Wisconsin include:</p><p>A calculator is a great first step, but closing cost structures and rate pricing vary by credit score, equity, and market timing. Rob Miller will analyze your current mortgage terms and present a clear comparison of your refinancing options.</p><ul><li>Lowering the Interest Rate: Reducing your rate is the most common way to save on interest and lower monthly payments.</li><li>Shortening the Loan Term: Moving from a 30-year fixed to a 15-year fixed mortgage to pay off the balance faster and build equity quickly.</li><li>Removing Private Mortgage Insurance (PMI): If your home value has increased, refinancing can remove costly conventional PMI.</li><li>Converting Rate Type: Switching from an Adjustable-Rate Mortgage (ARM) to a stable Fixed-Rate loan.</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><h2>Refinance FAQs</h2><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What is a refinance break-even point?</p><p class="faq-a">A: Your refinance break-even point is the number of months it takes for your monthly mortgage savings to equal the closing costs of the refinance. For example, if your closing costs are $3,000 and you save $150 per month, your break-even point is 20 months. If you plan to stay in the home longer than 20 months, refinancing is financially beneficial.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What are typical closing costs for a refinance?</p><p class="faq-a">A: Refinance closing costs generally range from 1% to 3% of the loan amount. They cover services like appraisal, title insurance, underwriting, and recording fees. Rob Miller can provide you with a detailed estimate of closing costs for your specific loan scenario.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: Does refinancing reset my 30-year term?</p><p class="faq-a">A: Refinancing typically involves choosing a new term, which can be 10, 15, 20, or 30 years. If you are 5 years into a 30-year loan and refinance into a new 30-year loan, you do reset the clock. However, you can also choose a shorter term (like a 15-year or 20-year) to pay off the home faster, or make extra principal payments to shorten your payoff timeline.</p></div></div><div class="cta"><h2>Ready to Optimize Your Home Loan?</h2><p>Let</p><span class="btn">Schedule My Refinance Consultation</span></div></body></html>